package armdemo

// A LIST OF UNIONS WHOSE ARM IS A POINTER (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.6, §2.9,
// §3.1): an element's set arm is the pointer edge itself, visited where the
// element sits, so two elements naming one node number it once and a node
// reached from no other field is still this root's to number, place and cook.

table Node { v int32 }

union Slot
{
    node  *Node
    plain int32
}

table Ring
{
    items []Slot
    after int32
}

// A LIST OF UNIONS WHOSE ARM IS AN ARRAY OF POINTERS, and a BOUNDED ARRAY of
// the same unions (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.6, §3.1): the arm's slot loop runs
// inside the element loop, so the two indexes are two spellings, and slot k
// of element i names element i's node and not element k's. Each element's
// slots hold distinct nodes, so a slot read off the wrong element is a node
// never numbered.

union Slots
{
    many  [..2]*Node
    plain int32
}

table Rack
{
    items []Slots
    after int32
}

table Tray
{
    entries [..2]Slots
    after   int32
}
